<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n2669" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">an-no</span></b>  (better <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">adn-</span></b> ), āre, v. n.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>To swim to</i>, <i>toward</i>, or <i>along;</i> constr. with the dat., <i>ad</i>, or acc.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b> With <i>dat.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terrae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 6, 358</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ei insulae crocodili non adnant,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					8, 25, 38, § 93</span></i>
			 Jan.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			With <i>ad</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad litus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					7, 8, 7</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(g).</b>
			With <i>acc.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pauci milites, qui naves adnare possent,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Caes.
					B. C. 2, 44</span></i>
			.—<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: plures adnabunt thynni, * <i><span class="en">Hor. S. 2,
				5, 44</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quod ubique gentium est, ad eam urbem posset
					adnare,</span>”
				<i>come to</i>, <i>approach</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Rep. 2, 4</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>To swim with</i> or <i>along
			with</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pedites adnantes equis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 14, 29</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
